      "id": "flax-journey",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "LESS FRICTION, MORE GAME",
      "body": "We are using Flax for KERN and modifying the engine as the project exposes what we need from it. I care a perhaps unreasonable amount about how tools look and feel, but that attention has a practical purpose: every confusing interaction, awkward panel and lost selection breaks momentum for me and my co-founder. The less the editor gets in our way, the more time we have for the actual game.\n\nThis work is part design exercise, part production infrastructure. We are rebuilding our stack with the knowledge earned on earlier projects, focusing first on the interactions we repeat all day: transforms, hierarchy behavior, properties, docking, navigation and content browsing.",
